section: rts
synopsis: Fix heap corruption under the nonmoving GC when copying boxed arrays
issues: #27376
mrs: !16481
description:
  The out-of-line code paths for `copyArray#` and `copyMutableArray#` (used
  whenever the element count is not a compile-time constant) did not push the
  overwritten destination elements to the nonmoving collector's update
  remembered set. Under `--nonmoving-gc` (`+RTS -xn`) the concurrent mark
  could then miss live objects and sweep them, causing silent heap corruption
  or crashes such as "internal error: ... object entered". Array copies with
  a constant element count and the small-array variants were not affected.
